    "created_at": "2023-02-03T10:21:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-02-03T10:21:17Z",
    "body": "This makes sense, but I'd go further and say that we need other ways of expressing semantic relationships more generally, especially within the document. There may be good reasons why rel is constrained to elements that are associated with http requests, and I'm fine with that, but not all content relationships are about http.\r\n\r\nFor example, if a heading 'belongs to' a list, then some kind of attribute could express this unambiguously. (Yes, I know that assistive tech has heuristics to figure this out, but why should ATs need to use heuristics? Why not be explicit?).\r\n\r\nSee:\r\nhttps://discourse.wicg.io/t/proposal-general-relationship-attribute-for-non-link-semantic-relationships/6123",
